  "question": {
    "text": "A small object at rest, absorbs a light pulse of power <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mW</mi></math> and duration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ns</mi></math>. Assuming speed of light as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The momentum of the object becomes equal to :",
    "image": null
